Z||000011||Kevin-84SE||01-25-2001||06:23 PM||||Yes Josh, that was me at the Rutland MA Fiero Show. (-:<P>Here is a recent picture of my car it's kind of in pieces right now, I turned the back wall into a door so that I could keep the car in a warmer room to work on it.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/open.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/closed.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Kevin-84SE||01-26-2001||11:05 PM||||jerpro,  I don't have blue prints or anything, I made the VU meters back in 84 and it was mostly my own creation. I can try to describe how I made it. <BR>For the electronics, I started with a kit from Radio Shack but it only provided for 8 LED's so I added a chip (LM3914 which is a 10  LED display driver chip) I needed the amp from the radio shack kit to filter the speaker output to provide a good signal to the LM3914. <BR>The LED's are a 10 rectangular LED inline package, the lens I got at a surplus store, the lens from a digital clock would probably work. the switch came out of a broken alarm clock and the panel is a piece of plastic cut to fit using the ash tray as a template and painted flat black. <BR>If I was to make one now, I would use 2 LM3916's (display drivers) in place of the LM3914 and 20 LED's per side, a simple OP AMP would probable do fine to filter the input to the display drivers.<P>   I hope this helps.<BR>   Kevin ||||reg||1
Z||000013||TheFiero64||01-27-2001||05:06 PM||||Why have you taken your Fiero all apart? It looked perfect the last time I saw it.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||5
Z||000014||FieroMaster88||01-27-2001||05:08 PM||||Cool, those are sweet!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
Z||000015||Kevin-84SE||01-28-2001||12:43 AM||||Thanks Josh, <P>   It's not really all apart but I found the drivers side rear wheel bearing was bad so I had to replace that. I also wanted to install  new seals in the trany, I put in the roller bearing seals. I took the rear bumper off because I have never had it off and I wanted to check for rust I didn't find much except for the e-brake cables, water must have gotten under the rubber and the metal started to rust. I think I got to it in time. Also taking the rear bumper off made it easier to remove the peanut shells from my space frame, apparently mice must have thought that my space frame was a great place to store their nuts. I am sure glad they didn't make it into the interior, they got into my wife's 300ZX and made a nest in the heater fan, that stunk for a long time. I took the rocker panels off because they need to be repainted, they were never clear coated. I am doing a few other minor things, I don't drive it in the winter so I figured it would be a good time to check everything over. It should be in great shape by the time the weather gets nice. <P>   Kevin||||reg||7
